.policy "bandit-b306-mktemp-q" revision 1
.guests off
.description "Use tempfile.mkstemp() or NamedTemporaryFile instead of tempfile.mktemp(); mktemp returns a name another process can claim before you create the file."
.language python
.mode steer
.scope include "**/*.py"
// Generated from today's JSON by docs/rule-syntax/site/translate.py. Display only: not compiled or run.

#include "python/names.rr"

// B306(n): a finding at node n, from clause `bandit:B306`.
// Each rule below is one way the JSON `rule` can match.
// The JSON `constraints` on F are added to every rule.
.violation B306(at: node) "Replace tempfile.mktemp with mkstemp or NamedTemporaryFile, which create the file atomically."
    suppress nosec "B306"
B306(n) :- n ~ `$F($$$ARGS)`, (sym_of(F, "tempfile.mktemp") ; F ~ `tempfile.mktemp`).
